Start the server:
/challenge/server
Open another terminal and test the web server:
curl -v http://challenge.localhost/blob
Read the server source code:
cat /challenge/server

The server constructs the requested file path using:

requested_path = app.root_path + "/files/" + path

The path value is controlled by the user, and there is no validation to prevent ../ sequences.

The intended directory is:
/challenge/files/

Using ../ allows us to move outside this directory.

Request the flag using path traversal:
curl --path-as-is http://challenge.localhost/blob/../../flag

The server receives:

/challenge/files/../../flag

which resolves to:

/flag
The server returns the flag.
Vulnerability

The application directly concatenates the user-controlled path with the /files/ directory without validating the resulting path.

The --path-as-is option is required because it prevents curl from normalizing the ../ sequences before sending the request.

